==Post-match==
{{Multiple image
| direction         = vertical
| width             = 220
| image1            = LFC Parade 2019 01.jpg
| image2            = UCL trophy at anfield museum.jpg
| caption1          = Liverpool players on an open-top bus, parading the Champions League trophy through the streets of Liverpool the day after the final
| caption2          = The 2019 Champions League trophy in the club museum
| align             = 
| total_width       = 
}}

Liverpool won their sixth European Cup and their second of the Champions League era.<ref name="NYT-Live"/> The club surpassed Barcelona and Bayern Munich, each with five titles, and ranks third behind Real Madrid (13) and [[AC Milan|Milan]] (7) for overall European titles.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0252-0e99c19b0df2-c2e63df5c79b-1000--liverpool-beat-tottenham-to-win-sixth-european-cup/ |title=Liverpool beat Tottenham to win sixth European Cup |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=1 June 2019 |access-date=1 June 2019 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20190602180220/https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/season=2019/matches/round=2000984/match=2025486/postmatch/report/ |archive-date=2 June 2019 }}</ref> Liverpool defender Virgil van Dijk was named the man of the match by UEFA for his leadership and interventions to break up Tottenham's attacks.<ref name="MOTM"/>

Liverpool returned to England the day after the final and celebrated their victory by parading the trophy around Liverpool in an open-top double-decker bus. The parade began at [[Allerton, Liverpool|Allerton Maze]] and continued for 8 miles (13 kilometres) towards the city centre, ending on the [[Liverpool Maritime Mercantile City|Liverpool Strand]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.liverpoolecho.co.uk/whats-on/whats-on-news/liverpool-fc-premier-league-champions-16244037|title=Full route and timetable announced for Liverpool victory parade|last=Kirwin|first=Ellen|date=2 June 2019|website=liverpoolecho|access-date=3 June 2019}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-merseyside-48472068|title=Crowds number 750,000 at Liverpool parade|work=BBC Sport|date=2 June 2019|access-date=3 June 2019}}</ref> Police estimated the number of supporters to be approximately 750,000, with the number of people lining the route causing the parade to last an additional two hours.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.liverpoolecho.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/pictures-liverpool-champions-league-parade-16368128|title=Unbelievable pictures show HUGE crowds for Liverpool's CL parade|last=Koncienzcy|first=Rebecca|date=2 June 2019|website=liverpoolecho|access-date=3 June 2019}}</ref>

===Subsequent matches===
As champions, Liverpool faced Chelsea (winners of the 2019 UEFA Europa League Final) in the [[2019 UEFA Super Cup]], held on 14 August. Liverpool won the match 5–4 on penalties after the game had ended 2–2 after extra time.<ref>{{cite news |title=Adrian the hero as Liverpool beat Chelsea on penalties to win Super Cup |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/49332825 |date=14 August 2019 |access-date=14 August 2019 |work=BBC Sport}}</ref> Representing Europe, Liverpool also took part in the [[2019 FIFA Club World Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |date=3 June 2019 |title=Club World Cup: Liverpool to play tournament in Qatar in December |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/48504200 |work=BBC Sport |access-date=4 June 2019 }}</ref> Liverpool went on to win their first Club World Cup title, defeating Mexican club [[C.F. Monterrey|Monterrey]] 2–1 in the semi-finals and Brazilian club [[Clube de Regatas do Flamengo|Flamengo]] 1–0 after extra time in the [[2019 FIFA Club World Cup final|final]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Hunter |first=Andy |date=18 December 2019 |title=Firmino's injury-time winner sends Liverpool into Club World Cup final |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2019/dec/18/monterrey-liverpool-fifa-club-world-cup-semi-final-match-report |work=The Guardian |access-date=18 December 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/firmino-writes-liverpool-into-club-world-cup-history |title=Firmino writes Liverpool into Club World Cup history |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=21 December 2019 |access-date=21 December 2019}}</ref>

